  "result": "The rule for LVMC_11_52_040_A is written and the gate returned **`OK`** on the first run (1 of 6), with all six witnesses giving their planned verdicts.\n\n**The rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_52_040_A.lean`):\n- **Subject:** a vehicle under the vehicle aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **When it applies:** the vehicle is parked (at rest for `p.standing_min_duration`, speed at or below `p.halt_speed_tolerance`), it is in a roadway, and no `angle_parking` regulatory sign governs a travel region it occupies.\n- **The duty:** the subject belongs to the traffic aggregate (`DEF-NRS-484A-285::traffic`), and in every travel region it occupies, its heading lines up with that region's direction. \"Lines up\" means the dot product of the two is at least `p.parked_heading_cos`.\n\n**The witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_52_040_A.lean`): an eastbound curbside lane inside an eastbound roadway. The car stands at (100, 2) facing west (forbid), east (permit) or north (branch_1). Scenes are 10 s apart, and only 80–140 s is judged, so the 60 s parked window is always fully covered. In idle the car drives at 1 m/s. In branch_2 an angle_parking sign governs the lane.\n\n**One gap for the plan**, also in `task_result.md`:\n- **Problem:** the node says the duty covers every travel region \"not an intersection\", but it doesn't claim an intersection atom, so I couldn't write that exclusion. The rule covers every occupied travel region.\n- **Effect:** a vehicle standing in an intersection, or in any region without a set direction, gets **unknown** instead of being exempt. That's also why the witnesses give the roadway a direction; without one, permit would come out unknown.\n- **Fix, if wanted:** the plan should claim `st.intersection` on span s4 and add a scenario for it.\n\nI declared no narrowings.",
